pable of  sailing thousands of miles around the  indian ocean  another accusation leveled against  europeans is that they  quote destroyed native culture but let's  look for a moment at how cultural  contact actually works  the simple fact is that when a good idea  comes along which clearly increases  living standards  people tend to adopt it and who is to  say that such  adaptation is bad native americans were  quick to adapt many useful old world  ideas which europeans had brought with  them  most of these had been adopted by  europeans from other old world cultures  why grind corn laboriously by hand for  several hours a day  when you can use millstones instead why  hunt with a bow and arrow when you can  use a rifle  why not domesticate cattle why refuse to  adopt the wheel for goodness sake  by the time columbus sets sail the old  world had dozens of clear technological  and institutional advantages which for  the most part  new world populations were eager to  adopt this made it inevitable that new  world society would be changed  once sustained contact was initiated  there is therefore little real mystery  of what happened to the native americans  as a culture  they were not exterminated at the behest  of any concerted  ideology of hatred or european  superiority  after the initial epidemics and in spite  of a few sensational wars and  small-scale massacres  remaining native americans adopted so  many old world customs  that most were gradually assimilated  into a new culture  this culture was mostly european in  british north america  but it was much more hybrid in places  like mexico and peru  where indigenous population density was  highest  many native americans converted to  christianity and took up farming  hundreds of thousands intermarried  further attesting to the ability of  average people of both  quote races to get along despite the  prejudices of pre-modern society  only a small proportion of native  americans stayed wild enough to be  placed on 